# Git operations

Source: `docs/governance/repository-operational-canon.md`.

- The trusted base is `integration/release-product-a-b`, fast-forward only.
- Product work happens in a worktree. Keep the main checkout on the trusted base.
- One concern per pull request.
- `/tmp` and `recovery/*` are not a source of truth.
- Commit only when the user asks. Message shape: `scope: summary`.
- Do not push unless the user asks.
- Before a product pull request, `make repo-health` is green.
- A pull request states the change, the checks that were run, and any blocking migration.
